WEBVTT

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:13.960
<i>The smell of summer grass...</i>

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:28.820
<i>White clouds with the slight breeze.</i>

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:35.820
<i>One person,</i>

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:39.450
<i>and another,</i>

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.740
<i>Hybrid Child.</i>

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.360
Hey Kuroda, are you there?

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:46.510
Success, success! It went well!

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.220
That was amazing! The aim was perfect too!

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.180
Kuroda, you! Don't mess with me!

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:54.210
What are you doing? That's an important part!

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:58.510
Shut up! Time after time, you're always making
lame things!

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:02.080
Seya! You should stop going along with him
every time!

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:06.160
Sorry, sorry, but it was really well done...

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:08.650
So, Tsukishima...

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.070
What do you want?

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:14.480
What's that?

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:17.050
If I don't want anything I can't come, is it?

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:17.990
Eh?

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:19.320
What,

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:21.840
are you jealous of Seya?

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:24.760
Okay, okay, calm down.

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:27.650
Aren't we all childhood friends here?

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.540
Let's just all get along.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:35.530
<i>Three houses lined side by side.</i>

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.720
<i>Even though our social classes are all different,</i>

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.820
<i>because we were all of the same age...</i>

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:48.360
Here, Tsukishima, it's your favourite Hiyoko buns.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:46.080
One person...

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.250
Hiyo buns?

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.170
<i>and another...</i>

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:52.850
Look here, wasn't I the one who brought those!?

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:51.690
<i>and another...</i>

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:55.110
<i>became childhood friends.</i>

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:11.670
By the way, Tsukishima-sama...

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:13.570
On this occasion,

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.900
please accept my sincerest congratulations upon
your official inauguration as a Minister.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:20.010
Huh?

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:23.860
Oh...

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:27.710
Actually, the situation is so unstable right now,

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:31.170
and with the clan being restructured...

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.590
...to think they chose you of all people to become
the Minister.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:44.770
The clan must be really short of talented people.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:49.000
Commit suicide! This is an order!

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:50.460
I'm sick of hearing that.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.940
If I keep obeying every word you say,

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.680
no matter how many lives I have, it won't be enough.

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:01.630
Kuroda!

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:04.800
What's with that guy?

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:07.030
Always making fun of me.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:13.180
If... if he hates me that much, he should just
make it clear!

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:15.000
That's not true, right?

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:19.290
Frankly, I hate this bun.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.040
Whenever I eat this, it sticks to the back of my teeth.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:25.880
Kuroda hates sweet things too.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:32.730
In that case, why do you think he has this
stocked up in his house?

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.830
Something like that, don't make me say it.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:51.520
<i>Even during the times we lazed around and
bickered over minor things,</i>

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:58.430
<i>the world, as our clan knew it, was falling into chaos.</i>

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:16.050
<i>The collapse of Shogunate feudalism,</i>

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:22.710
<i>the forming of a rebel group who wished for
a country with imperial rule.</i>

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.770
The Shogun saw that things weren't going well
and disappeared without a trace.

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:36.310
I heard that the Edo castle was handed over.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:41.750
Despite his initial bravado, doesn't this mean that
he only wants to save his own clan?

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:42.930
This is no joke!

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:45.400
They made use of our clan,

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:47.840
but now that he has no more use for us,
we're being tossed aside?

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:53.010
<i>Our clan, which has been made use of and
abandoned,</i>

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.440
<i>has lost its leader,</i>

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:58.530
<i>and is being dealt with like a rebel army.</i>

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:01.850
<i>War is approaching.</i>

00:06:03.890 --> 00:06:07.570
To be honest, for someone like me to become a
Minister of this clan,

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:09.780
I'm still confused about it.

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:13.880
About that...

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:17.840
It's a huge honor to be chosen by the Lord himself
as his Minister,

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:21.170
but whether I'm able to carry out this
important duty...

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:25.780
Rather, if you are born into the Minister's family,

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:28.330
you'll become a Minister no matter how stupid
you are.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:31.890
Regardless of what thoughts you have, you became
the Minister.

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:34.660
Make sure you do your job properly.

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:36.970
War is breaking out soon, right?

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:41.840
If your orders aren't firm enough, even the easiest
of battles can't be won.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.310
The ones who'll be troubled during the battles
are us, your subordinates.

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:45.350
That...

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:48.250
...I understand.

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:52.610
But, the responsibility is just too heavy...

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:54.520
Huh?

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:58.850
You...

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:02.570
Why do you think you were born into such a good
household and given such a good life?

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:06.260
Isn't that the price for a job with that
responsibility?

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:11.910
Do something about it before you whine
and complain.

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:14.110
It's not about whether you can do it or not,

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:15.840
"I'll do it!"

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.210
That's your duty.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:22.620
After we're done with this mess, feel free to
complain or cry to me.

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:25.030
Heh, or is it that...

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:28.180
you're telling me that you don't have that courage?

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:30.290
What was that!?

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:32.130
Because you're such a coward...

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.830
<i>How should I phrase this...</i>

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:34.240
Coward, coward!

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:38.580
<i>Kuroda really knows how to handle Tsukishima.</i>

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:39.360
When I set my mind to it, I can do anything!

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:40.450
Oh?...

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:43.990
If you don't even do it even when you can, it's the
same as being not able to.

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:46.680
I can do it! I'll definitely do it!

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:55.350
Yes, well said. Good boy, good boy.

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:00.570
<i>No,</i>

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:03.310
<i>maybe he isn't that good a handling him after all.</i>

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:32.980
<i>One person, and another, and another.</i>

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:39.390
<i>Always together. </i>

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:45.270
<i>Since then,</i>

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:48.780
<i>forever.</i>

00:10:14.810 --> 00:10:17.180
What is this room?

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:23.250
Is that your new puppet doll?

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:26.550
It's a doll with intelligence.

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:27.210
Huh?

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:29.910
It might look like a normal doll at first,

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:32.610
but if you shower it with care and love,

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:35.350
it will grow up like a child and become bigger.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.060
Interesting, isn't it?

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:40.670
What's with that?

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:43.180
There's no way something like that can be...

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:54.530
Say,

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:56.680
What?

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:04.090
Somehow, the face of this doll,

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:05.840
doesn't it look like me?

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:07.790
Can't be!

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:09.870
Of all the faces, why must it be yours...

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:18.790
Ah, it true.

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:21.840
It's exactly like Tsukishima's when he was little.

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:27.460
If I made a Tsukishima doll who is honest,

00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:30.040
I thought you might be able to improve yourself
in various ways.

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:31.820
Be thankful towards me.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:34.080
Don't mess with me!

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:35.470
Something like this...!

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:37.520
Ah! What are you doing?

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:39.520
That should be my line!

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:42.770
What are you trying to do, making someone else
into your experimental material?

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:44.460
Stop shouting so much!

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:47.700
Why does it always have to be me?

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:51.110
You bastard, just go and die!

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:56.920
You keep telling me to die whenever you see
my face.

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:01.880
But honestly, what will you do if I really died?

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:06.200
Wh-what will I do...?

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:08.220
Let go.

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:10.410
If it's the Minister's order,

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:14.440
then a lowly soldier like me can only obey.

00:12:15.900 --> 00:12:18.600
Stop saying it that way...

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:21.170
Let go of my hands.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:23.270
Kuroda,

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:25.710
don't trouble Tsukishima like that.

00:12:26.130 --> 00:12:27.020
My hands...

00:12:32.170 --> 00:12:33.540
Oh well,

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:36.600
and I thougt I was finally making progress with it.

00:12:37.510 --> 00:12:39.660
I'll have to start all over again, isn't it?

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:41.400
I'm leaving.

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:45.810
Tsukishima, don't you have to give that to him?

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:47.140
What is it?

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:57.600
The tree in the middle of my courtyard.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:01.180
The wind was really strong last night,

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:04.650
In the morning I saw a broken branch

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:07.590
and I thought it might be good for re-planting.

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:10.820
You like flowers, right?

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:15.070
That's why...

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:21.970
...for you.

00:13:25.850 --> 00:13:26.690
About that...

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:29.400
...thank you.

00:13:35.480 --> 00:13:37.060
Oh, so you were here!

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:38.830
Finally found you!

00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:42.590
Bad news, seems like the enemy is attacking
from Edo.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:45.990
We think they split into 3 groups,

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:47.620
one is headed for Kazusa,

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:49.450
one is headed for Uchinomiya

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:51.420
and one is headed for Dewa.

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:55.490
<i>My heart is...</i>

00:13:56.100 --> 00:14:01.350
They are making use of our label as "rebels" and
attacking us with that excuse.

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:03.460
What a mess!

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:06.620
<i>...making a racket.</i>

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:09.350
<i>I feel horrible.</i>

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:13.270
Anyway, please return to the castle to
give your orders!

00:14:23.070 --> 00:14:25.870
<i>Although nobody will ever speak of it...</i>

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:33.560
There are 5 points where we're vulnerable
to invasions.

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:37.320
I'll now assign a squad to each point.

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:42.930
The commander shall be I, Tsukishima!

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:46.920
<i>Probably everyone in our clan is well aware...</i>

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:51.650
Tsushima point, first sqaud leader, Seya!

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:52.960
Yes sir!

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:57.270
<i>Our clan which had unknowingly become
a rebel faction...</i>

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:03.130
Shirasaka point, first squad leader, Kuroda!

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:04.100
Yes sir!

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:09.450
<i>What can we do to hear the words of victory?</i>

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:14.810
<i>We can only pray.</i>

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:19.010
Ooshima point, first squad leader...

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:25.250
Watering the cherry blossoms I received,
I'll leave it to you.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:30.410
You can enter my house as you please...

00:15:31.270 --> 00:15:32.620
Since it was a good branch,

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:35.790
if possible, I would like to graft it onto a fruit
tree or something.

00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:39.260
Got it.

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:41.710
What's wrong?

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:43.600
Staring to feel nervous?

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:50.280
What's this?

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:54.400
you aren't going to tell me "die" or
"commit suicide" this time?

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:59.080
If you die right now, it will cause trouble
for others.

00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:04.210
That is so, isn't it.

00:16:06.050 --> 00:16:06.660
See you then.

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:10.150
Kuroda.

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:14.380
Well...

00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:15.900
...be careful.

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:20.850
Be sure to return.

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:04.630
What?

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:08.040
I wonder.

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:17.590
I'll exchange this for yours.

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:19.240
Huh?

00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:21.370
Because you're a coward,

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:22.890
I'm giving it to you as a protection charm.

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:26.220
Whenever you are on the verge of breaking down,

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:29.190
or when you need someone to cheer you up,

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:33.960
there's a note sewn into the end of it.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.050
Take it out and read it.

00:17:47.380 --> 00:17:47.980
Kuroda...

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:49.960
We have a long way to go,

00:17:50.770 --> 00:17:53.110
so pull yourself together, Minister.

00:17:53.820 --> 00:17:54.330
See you.

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:55.750
Squad leader!

00:17:56.480 --> 00:17:57.310
I'm coming now.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:24.430
"Only idiots will look"

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:33.330
Kuroda!

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:33.970
Say,

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:37.540
don't you think the Minister is an idiot?

00:18:37.710 --> 00:18:38.370
Huh?

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:54.140
What is it?

00:18:57.470 --> 00:19:01.180
If...if we just pray...

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:05.930
You beat around the bush too much.

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:11.170
Why can't you just tell him that you want to
protect him?

00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:14.320
Shut up!... I'll hit you!

00:19:15.640 --> 00:19:18.600
<i>Let's end this war before the next year when this
cherry blossom blooms,</i>

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:22.540
<i>and then let's go flower-viewing again.</i>

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:25.520
<i>Did you know?</i>

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:38.060
<i>Cherry blossoms are at their best on the night
just before their buds bloom.</i>

00:19:38.930 --> 00:19:43.820
<i>In the darkness, against the moonlight, as if it
were a mist of pink...</i>

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:47.680
<i>That is very beautiful.</i>

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:23.600
Wait a minute!

00:20:23.600 --> 00:20:24.230
Kuroda!

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:30.580
Why must Tsukishima... commit suicide!?

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:33.020
Kuroda, calm down!

00:20:33.070 --> 00:20:34.770
Your wounds will re-open!

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:36.430
Shut up! Don't touch me!

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:38.620
This is no joke!

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:40.600
Why must it be Tsukishima!?

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:41.470
It can't be helped!

00:20:41.850 --> 00:20:42.340
Hey!

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:44.660
Kuroda! Stop moving around!

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:48.160
Our clan has been defeated!

00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:51.890
In order to protect our Lord's life,

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:54.440
someone has to bear the responsibility.

00:20:56.370 --> 00:21:01.380
All Ministers who are older than Tsukishima
have died during the battles.

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:03.500
Who else do we have, besides him?

00:21:04.170 --> 00:21:05.370
In that case, I will...

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:09.050
Your death is worthless to them!

00:21:15.090 --> 00:21:16.750
I'm in pain too.

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:19.950
Tsukishima was very courageous,

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:23.900
to have suggested it himself.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:28.060
Then, when is that?

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:33.200
Tomorrow.

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:49.040
<i>Tsukishima...</i>

00:22:36.890 --> 00:22:41.780
Tsumetai sono taion wo kanjiteru

00:22:36.890 --> 00:22:41.780
Feeling the coolness of your body temperature

00:22:41.780 --> 00:22:46.390
Kasanaru kage ni mo himitsu madotte

00:22:41.780 --> 00:22:46.390
Even the overlapping shadows hide secrets

00:22:55.610 --> 00:22:59.570
Yurari, Yurari

00:22:55.610 --> 00:22:59.570
Swaying, swaying,

00:23:00.350 --> 00:23:04.230
Kokoro ga yureteru

00:23:00.350 --> 00:23:04.230
My heart is swaying

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:14.010
Zutto onaji basho wo motomete

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:14.010
Always seeking for the same place

00:23:14.690 --> 00:23:18.850
Kagami no youni utsushidashite

00:23:14.690 --> 00:23:18.850
Reflecting like a mirror

00:23:18.850 --> 00:23:23.520
Tashikametai setsuna no kioku

00:23:18.850 --> 00:23:23.520
The sad memories I want to confirm

00:23:23.520 --> 00:23:32.460
Sono karada katachi sae futari no mono dakara

00:23:23.520 --> 00:23:32.460
because the silhouette of that body belongs to the two of us

00:23:33.810 --> 00:23:38.640
Tsumetai sono taion wo kanjite

00:23:33.810 --> 00:23:38.640
Feeling the coolness of your body temperature

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:43.240
Chiisai hana he te omoitakushite

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:43.240
Entrusting our feelings to little flowers

00:23:43.240 --> 00:23:46.340
Tsuki no hikari no shita

00:23:43.240 --> 00:23:46.340
Beneath the moonlight

